Package: ezrmodel
Type: Package
Title: Single-Line Modelling and Clustering for Consumer Data
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person("Andreas", "Schellewald", email = "aschellewald@acm.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Turns the advanced-analytics tasks that research and insights
    professionals reach for into single-line helpers that return a complete,
    diagnosable result. Find what drives a target variable (a consensus of
    correlation, regression, relative-weights, random-forest and factor
    importance), segment data with clustering and read off the diagnostics and
    cluster profiles, reduce dimensions, fit and tidy regressions, and run
    grouped hypothesis tests. Designed around a session 'default dataset' so the
    same pattern works across surveys, social and ecommerce data. Also turns open
    text into tidy term frequencies, tf-idf, topic models and extractive
    summaries, and checks latent structure with scale reliability, exploratory
    factor analysis and confirmatory models. Selects predictors with stepwise or
    penalised regression, compares fitted models on common metrics, and embeds
    data in two dimensions with UMAP or t-SNE.
